      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ERIN JO (2) sets the standard after resuming with a sound third at Wyong, beaten just under two lengths, and she is proven around 1400m with one win from two starts at the distance. Her run in The Roses (G2) last campaign gives her form a stronger base than most of these, and the weight relief from her first-up run adds to the appeal. Go close. MODERNIST (6) is the clear danger after winning a Mdn at Muswellbrook by just over three lengths, though this is harder company. Expected to run the trip and looks to have more to give. ABOVE THE LAW (1) was disappointing as a well-supported favourite at Kembla Grange, but the drop out of BM64 grade and his 1400m record keep him in the mix. No shock to see him return to winning form. EXPLOSIVE TYCOON (8) comes back from Saturday company after being beaten only three lengths in a Class 3 at Randwick, with his close Class 2 second at Taree making him a credible place hope.",
